back('ribs', 'far', "A photograph taken with a long lens from low over a wet tidal flat, looking straight down the middle of a sea strait just after a storm. Only the far end of the strait is in the picture, everything further than about two kilometres from the camera: two rows of colossal pale stone blades stand out of the sea, one row on the left and one on the right, each blade hundreds of metres tall, broad at the foot and curving inward to a hooked tip like the rib of a whale, the two rows leaning toward each other over the water. Six or seven blades on each side recede one behind another toward the horizon, each paler and bluer than the one in front and the last ones almost lost in sea haze. Black weed darkens the foot of every blade up to one level tide line, and white surf breaks round the feet. Between the rows the sea runs out to a level horizon, slate green with far white lines of surf, under heavy slate-grey storm cloud that is breaking apart, with a bright silver gap low over the sea in the middle. The horizon lies at the middle of the frame. Below it there is only open sea, with thin wet sand along the very bottom edge: no near rocks, no cliffs at the sides of the frame, no pools, no blade nearer than two kilometres.", 0, 'anchor-coast-1.jpg', 'the far end of the strait, which the frames leave empty', group=1)
sheet('ribs', 'blade', "One whole rib blade of the strait, seen square on from the side in an orthographic view: a colossal fin of weathered bone turned to stone, 300 metres tall, standing upright with its foot at the bottom of the frame and its tip at the top. It is broad at the foot, about 90 metres, narrows as it rises and hooks over to the right at the top like the rib of a whale, with one sharp edge and one thick rounded edge. Pale ivory and grey-cream, fluted along its whole length with long shallow grooves that follow its curve, pitted and flaked in patches, with dark water stains running down it, white streaks below small ledges where animals roost, rust-orange lichen in patches, one small natural arch worn through near the foot, and its lowest tenth covered in hanging black-olive weed up to one level line.", 0, 'plate-surf-1.jpg', 'one blade whole, for the shape, the fluting and the stains of the blades', 300, aspect='9:16', height=True, group=1)
ground('ribs', 'plate', "The floor of a sea strait at low tide, a piece 48 metres wide and 27 metres tall. Wet dark grey sand with ripple marks, long bars of shingle and pebbles, shallow braided channels where the last water drains across it, scattered stones from 0.2 to 1 metre, low clumps of black-olive weed lying flat, shell grit. The sand is dark and wet but there are no reflections of the sky on it and no standing pools.", 0, 'plate-surf-1.jpg', 'the tide flat of the lower half of the establishing picture', 48, asked=RG, group=2)
face('ribs', 'wall', "The foot of a colossal rib of pale stone at low tide, a face 40 metres wide and 40 metres tall. The top quarter is pale ledged ivory rock with rust-orange lichen and white runs of droppings. Below a ragged level weed line the rock is hung with ropes, straps and curtains of black, olive and amber seaweed in heavy clumps that hang straight down, glistening wet, with gaps of wet black barnacled rock between the clumps and thin runs of water.", 1, 'plate-surf-1.jpg', 'the weed-hung foot of the near left rib, for the establishing picture and the drowned one', 40, aspect='1:1', asked=RG, group=2)
face('ribs', 'colony', "The cliff where a colony of flying animals roosts, a face 40 metres wide and 40 metres tall, with no animals on it. Broken angular ledges of pale grey-white rock in rough steps of unequal depth and height, never even like a stair, white runs of droppings below every ledge, rust-orange and yellow lichen, untidy nests of dried black weed on the ledges, dark wet seams, and wet kelp at the foot.", 3, 'plate-surf-1.jpg', 'the stepped cliff of the colony', 40, aspect='1:1', asked=RG, group=2)
tile('ribs', 'shingle', DOWN + "a bed of wet pebbles and shingle on a tidal flat, about 2 metres across. Rounded grey, slate and pale pebbles from 2 to 10 centimetres, wet and dark, with coarse sand and shell grit between them and a few scraps of dark weed.", 0, 'plate-surf-1.jpg', 'the pebble beds of the tide flat', 2, asked=RG, group=3)
sheet('ribs', 'kitewing', "One kite-wing, an animal of an unknown world, standing, seen exactly from the side in an orthographic view, facing right, about 2.2 metres tall. It stands on two very long thin legs with knobbly joints, like a wading bird. Its body is small and lean under pale pinkish-cream skin. Its long neck hangs forward and down and ends, where a head would be, in nothing but a tuft of long pale wet tendrils. Two wings are folded along its back: long thin finger bones with leathery membrane between them, cream going to orange-tan and ragged at the trailing edge, the folded tips standing out behind it.", 2, 'ref-wader-1.jpg', 'the kite-wing whole in side view, for the shape of its one skin', 2.2, animal=True, group=1)
sheet('ribs', 'kitewing-front', "One kite-wing, an animal of an unknown world, standing, seen exactly from the front in an orthographic view, about 2.2 metres tall. It stands on two very long thin legs with knobbly joints, like a wading bird, feet apart. Its body is small and lean under pale pinkish-cream skin. Its long neck rises and bends forward and ends, where a head would be, in nothing but a tuft of long pale wet tendrils hanging down. Two wings are held half open at its sides: long thin finger bones with leathery membrane between them, cream going to orange-tan and ragged at the trailing edge.", 2, 'ref-wader-1.jpg', 'the same animal from the front, for its width and the set of its wings', 2.2, aspect='1:1', animal=True, asked=RS, group=3)
tile('ribs', 'hide', "A material texture, seen straight on: the skin of the body and neck of a lean long-legged flying animal, about 0.5 metres across. Thin pale pinkish-cream skin with a very short sparse down, fine wrinkles, goose-flesh pimples, faint blue-grey veins, low ridges where bones press through from beneath, wet patches and a few small scars. No feathers, no scales.", 2, 'ref-hide-1.jpg', 'the skin of the kite-wings, beside the wing membrane already made', 0.5, group=3)
