sheet('ribs', 'borewall-a', "One section of a tidal bore, a single breaking wall of sea water, seen square on from in front: a section 70 metres wide and 30 metres tall that runs out of the frame at the left and right edges. A dark green-grey face of water, glassy and streaked, its crest curling over toward the viewer along its whole length and throwing ragged spray upward, foam streaming down the face in long white veins, and a band of white churn at its foot. The light comes from behind the wave and from the right, so the thin lip of the crest glows pale green. The wall reaches from the left edge of the frame to the right edge; black is above it and below it only.", 4, 'plate-surf-1.jpg', 'the face of the bore, first section', 70, height=True, asked=RS, group=2)
sheet('ribs', 'borewall-b', "A second, different section of a tidal bore, a single breaking wall of sea water, seen square on from in front: a section 70 metres wide and 30 metres tall that runs out of the frame at the left and right edges. Here the crest has already pitched forward in the middle and is falling as a thick white curtain, with a hollow dark green tube open at the left and a smooth unbroken dark shoulder at the right, spray torn off the top by wind, foam veins on the face and a deep band of white churn at the foot. The light comes from behind the wave and from the right, so the thin lip of the crest glows pale green. The wall reaches from the left edge of the frame to the right edge; black is above it and below it only.", 4, 'plate-surf-1.jpg', 'the face of the bore, second section', 70, height=True, asked=RS, group=2)
onblack('ribs', 'spray', "A sheet of sixteen separate bursts of thrown sea spray in a grid of four columns and four rows, one burst in the middle of each cell with black between them and no lines between the cells. Each burst is about 8 metres across and different from the others: ragged plumes, fans and tall fingers of white droplets and mist thrown upward, dense at the root and torn to fine mist at the top, lit from behind and from the right.", 4, 'plate-surf-1.jpg', 'spray sprites for the bore and the surf', 8, tiled=False, asked=RS, group=3)
onblack('ribs', 'splash', "A sheet of sixteen separate small splashes of water in a grid of four columns and four rows, one splash in the middle of each cell with black between them and no lines between the cells. Each splash is about 0.6 metres across and different from the others: crowns of drops, arcs of drops, falling strings of drops, a single thrown sheet, and ring ripples seen from a low angle, lit from behind.", 2, 'plate-surf-1.jpg', 'splash sprites for the feeders and the pools', 0.6, tiled=False, asked=RS, group=3)
sheet('ribs', 'wingopen', "One wing of a kite-wing, an animal of an unknown world, fully spread and laid flat, seen from straight above: 2.4 metres long, its root at the left edge of the subject and its tip at the right, its leading edge at the top. Four long thin bone fingers fan out from the wrist, with thin leathery membrane stretched between them: cream near the root, going to orange and tan toward the trailing edge, which is torn and ragged, with a branching net of fine dark veins, small scars and wrinkles. No feathers, no hair.", 2, 'ref-tissue-1.jpg', 'one wing spread, for the membrane sheets of the feeders and the colony', 2.4, height=True, asked=RS, group=2)
sheet('ribs', 'carcass', "The drowned carcass of a kite-wing, an animal of an unknown world, long dead, seen square on, 3 metres tall: it hangs head down by one leg, caught at the top of the frame, the other leg bent out sideways, the long neck and its tuft of pale tendrils hanging straight down at the bottom. Shrivelled pale hide shrunk tight on the ribs and the leg bones, split open in holes that show bone, one wing torn to rags of membrane on thin finger bones, strands of dark weed caught on it and a few small pale crabs clinging to it.", 1, 'ref-hide-1.jpg', 'the drowned one, for its sagging skin', 3, aspect='1:1', height=True, animal=True, asked=RS, group=2)

